List a table created after the transaction started at its current schema.

A listing of the catalog (duckdb_tables(), duckdb_columns(),
information_schema, pg_catalog) shows each table any connection has loaded
at its schema as of the transaction's start, as a bind sees it. A table
created since has no schema that old: patch 0006 makes a bind of it fail the
transaction, and a listing failed the same way. Igloo lists the catalog's
tables on a session's own connection to check its statements' grants,
whenever DDL has run since the last listing, so a transaction block failed
its next statement whenever another session had created and read a table
since the block began, whatever tables the statement used. A listing, which
shows the catalog's tables as they are now, now shows such a table at its
current schema; a statement that reads or writes it still fails the
transaction.

